      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1353169193,
      "text": "Litsea monopetala is a plant in the family Lauraceae, native to southern China, the Indian Subcontinent, Indo-China, Peninsular Malaysia, Sumatra, and Java. In Nepal, it is found in the regions from the Terai to 1450 m, in Shorea robusta forest and tropical evergreen forest. In India it is found in Assam, Odisha, Eastern Himalayas, Maharashtra and Tamil Nadu (Coimbatore)."
    }
